00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000 00000000 # data | GDT null descriptor | Selector zero is deliberately unusable in protected mode.
11111111 11111111 00000000 00000000 00000000 10011010 11001111 00000000 # data | GDT flat 32-bit code descriptor | Base zero, limit FFFFF, access 9A, flags C; granularity expands the inclusive limit to FFFFFFFF, D=1 selects 32-bit code.
11111111 11111111 00000000 00000000 00000000 10010010 11001111 00000000 # data | GDT flat 32-bit data descriptor | Base zero, limit FFFFF, access 92, flags C; writable ring-zero data, with B=1 for a 32-bit stack.
00010111 00000000 00000000 01111111 00000000 00000000 # data | GDTR pointer | Limit 0017 is 24 descriptor bytes minus one; base is little-endian 00007F00.
00000111 00000001 00110000 01111111 00000000 00000000 # data | IDTR pointer | Limit 0107 is 33 eight-byte entries minus one; base is little-endian 00007F30.
